00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.000
Infectious diseases are as wide-ranging as

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.000
the microbes that cause them. We come in contact with pathogens every hour of the day. Some

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.390
pathogens even take up residence in our body, and we don't even know it until we feel sick.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:48.250
Our own microbial flora may become unbalanced. In this case, good bugs go bad, like a yeast

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:55.550
infection. Or we encounter known pathogens, like Salmonella, by eating contaminated foods.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:00.000
Or by boldly going where no human has gone before. We encounter diseases

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.810
that are new to us, like Ebola.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.610
Diseases can spread from one person to another

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.450
if the environment is right for transmission.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:15.700
Sometimes this can be as simple as a handshake.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.140
Some microbes, such as the ones that live

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:23.730
in our digestive tract, are beneficial to our well-being.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.520
Other microbes, however, have been our enemies

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.360
for thousands of years.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.750
history infectious diseases have wiped out huge populations in 1918 over 20

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:47.890
million people died from an influenza virus that swept the globe eventually we

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:52.130
realized that each disease seemed to have a perpetrator often with distinct

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.690
attributes such as speed and replicating or agility and beating our

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.000
immune cell defenses then we began to dramatically change the balance

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.620
in our favor. First came the concept of hygiene: washing with clean water and soap.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.410
Public health has improved dramatically thanks to fresh water supplies and

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:24.860
sanitation. The discovery of penicillin heralded the age of antibiotics. Antibiotics, along with

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.000
